{"explanation":"Count occurrences in the first array using a Map, then iterate through the second array, emitting a value only when a remaining first-array count is available and decrementing that count. This yields the multiset intersection without mutating either input. Finally, sort the emitted numbers numerically ascending.","code":"function solve(a, b) {
  const counts = new Map();
  for (const value of a) {
    counts.set(value, (counts.get(value) || 0) + 1);
  }

  const result = [];
  for (const value of b) {
    const remaining = counts.get(value) || 0;
    if (remaining > 0) {
      result.push(value);
      counts.set(value, remaining - 1);
    }
  }

  result.sort((x, y) => x - y);
  return result;
}"}

{"explanation":"Uses the Josephus recurrence: for m people, the survivor index among 0..m-1 is (survivor for m-1 people + k) mod m, with base 0 for one person. Iterating m from 2 to n gives the survivor label directly.","code":"function solve(n, k) {
